      "raw_result_body": "{\"what\":\"Aperture: a safe way to work in web systems that have no API. Compile a page into typed tools, then every change is a ticket: preview, check, commit, read-back, undo.\",\"kinds\":[\"form1\",\"devices\",\"residents\",\"vendors\"],\"how\":[\"Look first: find(kind, query). Names are not unique. Always use the key.\",\"To change something: apply(op, kind, key). If the rules allow it, it commits at once and returns a receipt.\",\"To look before you commit: delete or create with dry_run: true, then commit with plan_id.\",\"Some changes need the owner. You get status awaiting_approval and a plan_id. Poll get_plan. Never retry blindly.\",\"publish pushes staged changes to the outside world. It always needs the owner.\",\"A receipt has verified facts from a read-back. If verified is false, say so. Do not claim success.\",\"undo(receipt_id) reverses a change within the undo window. Published changes cannot be recalled.\",\"A refusal always lists next moves. Follow one of them.\",\"Web forms: compile_site(url) reads a page's forms (only hosts the operator authorized). Each form is a kind with key 'current'. Fill with apply({op:'update', patch}). Submit with publish, which always needs the owner. A CAPTCHA is a human step.\"],\"mandate\":{\"maxDeletesPerDay\":5,\"planTtlMs\":300000,\"undoWindowMs\":86400000}}",
